{"name":"Heavenly","hex":"#7eb2c5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Heavenly","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A female given name."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of heavenly."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Heavenly"}],"entries":[{"title":"Heaven","blocks":[{"text":"Heaven, or the Heavens, is a common religious cosmological or supernatural place where beings such as deities, angels, souls, saints, or venerated ancestors are said to originate, be enthroned, or reside. According to the beliefs of some religions, heavenly beings can descend to Earth or incarnate and earthly beings can ascend to Heaven in the afterlife or, in exceptional cases, enter Heaven without dying."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Paradiso_Canto_31_%28148200393%29.jpg/330px-Paradiso_Canto_31_%28148200393%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heaven","wikidata":"Q4489450"},{"title":"Heavenly (British band)","blocks":[{"text":"Heavenly are an English twee pop band, originally forming in Oxford, England in 1989. Amelia Fletcher (vocals/guitar), Mathew Fletcher, Peter Momtchiloff (guitar) and Robert Pursey (bass) were all previously members of Talulah Gosh, a key member of the C86 scene."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Heavenly_indie_1994.jpg/330px-Heavenly_indie_1994.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heavenly_(British_band)","wikidata":"Q944058"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/86/Beowulf_-_heofones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/86/Beowulf_-_heofones.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"